<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="e24a3cfe">&lt;p&gt;
    The work product focuses on understanding the needs of users in terms of learning resources, skills, development and
    delivery capacity, and capability. It also considers the environment requirements, learning platforms, tools, and
    channels, and how they will operate in relation to the learning program. Additionally, it addresses the technical
    specifications and roadmap for any tools that may impact training development, delivery, or end user devices, such as
    Learning Management Systems (LMS), internal systems, hosting solutions, policies, model office requirements, laptop and
    mobile policies, desktop setups, and cloud hosting.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Physical Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Space and Facilities:&lt;/em&gt; Adequate classrooms, laboratories, libraries, and other learning spaces should be
        available to accommodate learners and facilitate interactions.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Furniture and Equipment:&lt;/em&gt; Appropriate seating arrangements, desks, whiteboards, projectors, computers,
        internet access, and audiovisual aids are essential for engaging and interactive learning sessions.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Safety and Security:&lt;/em&gt; Providing a safe and secure environment through fire safety measures, emergency exit
        plans, surveillance systems, and controlled access to premises.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Digital Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Hardware:&lt;/em&gt; Computers, laptops, tablets, mobile devices, and network infrastructure need to be sufficient
        and up-to-date for students to access digital learning materials and online resources.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Software and Applications:&lt;/em&gt; Learning management systems (LMS), virtual classrooms, collaborative tools,
        educational software, and various applications should be available to facilitate content delivery, assessments, and
        collaboration.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Internet Connectivity:&lt;/em&gt; Reliable internet access with sufficient bandwidth is crucial for students and
        educators to access online content, participate in virtual classrooms, download/upload assignments, and engage in
        research.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Cybersecurity:&lt;/em&gt; Measures to protect digital infrastructure and data from unauthorized access, viruses,
        malware, and other cyber threats are necessary to safeguard privacy and maintain the integrity of learning
        materials.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Support Services:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Technical Support:&lt;/em&gt; A dedicated helpdesk or IT support team should be available to assist with
        troubleshooting technical issues, software glitches, connectivity problems, and other related concerns.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Learning Support:&lt;/em&gt; Access to learning resources, textbooks, reference materials, libraries, online
        databases, and academic support services such as tutoring, mentoring, and counseling should be provided to enhance
        the learning experience.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Accessibility:&lt;/em&gt; Providing accessibility for learners with disabilities including assistive technologies,
        accommodating physical spaces, and providing captioning, transcripts, and alternative formats for digital content.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;em&gt;Infrastructure Maintenance:&lt;/em&gt; Regular maintenance, updates, and repairs of physical and digital
        infrastructure to provide for its smooth functioning and longevity.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="b4453ace"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="f1f1503"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="3362a14d"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="3bfb8a6e">&lt;p&gt;
    To communicate the technical environment and data needs for learning development and deployment, while aligning the
    learning infrastructure with the requirements and capabilities of the users. Additionally, it assists in identifying
    any necessary new tools or platforms and gathering technical specifications for existing tools and systems that could
    influence learning development and delivery.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
